    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i guess i just worry about the money sitting there. like, if the escrow person is just holding all this large amount of cash and sensitive documents, it feels a bit risky. what actually happens if they lose it or if something goes wrong with that \"neutral\" person? is there any kind of protection for the buyer?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To alleviate concerns, escrow funds are typically held in a separate account by a licensed escrow agent or company, insured up to the full amount of the transaction, and audited regularly by regulatory bodies and the escrow agents themselves. If the escrow agent becomes insolvent or takes a breach of duty, an Investor Protection fund would likely be reviewed to repay losses. Additionally, in Washington, escrow officers are also regulated by the Washington State Department of Financial Institutions.",
      "source": "target",
